{{--
  PredictHQ mark.

  A probability, drawn. The ring is the full distribution and the filled
  arc is the part a forecast has claimed, swept to roughly 68%, which is
  one standard deviation and reads as "confident but not certain". The
  centre dot is the point estimate the arc is built around.

  It is an inline SVG rather than a glyph because the previous mark was a
  literal `◎` character: it rendered as a different shape on every
  platform, could not take the brand colour independently of its
  container, and disappeared entirely where the font lacked it.

  currentColor throughout, so one file serves the light nav, the dark
  nav, and the footer without a second copy. Size comes from the wrapper.
--}}
<svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" style="width:100%;height:100%;display:block">
  <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" opacity="0.28" />
  {{--
    Arc from 12 o'clock, swept clockwise ~245° (68% of the circle).
    Drawn with an explicit large-arc flag so the sweep is unambiguous.
  --}}
  <path
    d="M16 5 A11 11 0 1 1 6.5 21.5"
    stroke="currentColor"
    stroke-width="2.5"
    stroke-linecap="round"
  />
  <circle cx="16" cy="16" r="3.25" fill="currentColor" />
</svg>
